{"id": "tea:pravacanasara:1.20", "source": "src:pravacanasara", "location": {"ref": "1.20"}, "paraphrase": "For the omniscient there is no bodily pleasure or pain, because he has become beyond the senses; so it is to be understood.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "powers-experiences"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "concepts": ["cpt:kevala-jnana", "cpt:kevalibhukti"], "disputes": ["dsp:kevalin-eats"], "terms": ["trm:kevalin"], "notes": "Verse number moderate confidence; cited by Digambaras against the kevalin's eating.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pravacanasara:1.7", "source": "src:pravacanasara", "location": {"ref": "1.7"}, "paraphrase": "Conduct is indeed dharma; that dharma is declared to be equanimity (sama); equanimity is the state of the self free from delusion and agitation.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "consciousness-mind"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "terms": ["trm:dharma", "trm:samya"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-upayogas"], "practices": ["prc:samayika"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pravacanasara:1.80", "source": "src:pravacanasara", "location": {"ref": "1.80"}, "paraphrase": "Whoever knows the Arhat through his substance, qualities and modes knows his own self, and his delusion is destroyed.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "terms": ["trm:arhat"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-atmans"], "obstacles": ["obs:mithyatva"], "notes": "Verse number moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pravacanasara:3", "source": "src:pravacanasara", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "The third part, on conduct: the renunciant takes the sign 'like the newborn' — naked, with hair plucked out, without possessions — and keeps the twenty-eight root qualities; he is equal to friend and foe, to praise and blame, to clod and gold. In Jayasena's longer recension this part includes verses stating that women cannot take this sign in its fullness and are not liberated in that birth; these verses are absent from Amṛtacandra's recension.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "advanced", "stage_native": "śramaṇa"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice", "dispute"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "concepts": ["cpt:twenty-eight-mulagunas", "cpt:monastic-nudity", "cpt:strimukti"], "disputes": ["dsp:monastic-nudity", "dsp:women-caste-liberation"], "notes": "Chapter-level ref; the textual point about the two recensions is recalled with moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
